  "body": "## F12.9 — Program upgrade with state migration\n\nFrom the Phase 12 plan (`.opencode/plans/phase-12-platform-flexibility.md`, workstream C):\n\nVersioned snapshots and an optional `migrate` export. An upgrade runs on a probe instance first (the way checkpoints already do), commits only if the migrated state round-trips, and otherwise rolls back.\n\n**Exit:** a test upgrades a counter across a snapshot format change, and a deliberately failing upgrade leaves the old program running.\n\n**Coordination (2026-10-26 reprioritization, per Drew):** every id roadmap item now has its own GitHub issue, and priority encodes the order: (1) the path to Phase 12 — `now` + `priority/high`; (2) Phase 12 itself — `next`; (3) Phase 13 and long-term ideas — `priority/low`. The dashboard mirrors this list (org Project \"Developing Today\" #4, Area `id-train`; Grist Program roadmap, Area `id`). If this item turns out to be blocked, wrong, or superseded, park or close it with a note rather than letting it stall the queue — dropping an issue is always allowed; silently stalling is not.\n",
